    "summary": "Not all two-factor authentication methods are equally secure: FIDO2 hardware keys and passkeys offer the strongest, phishing-resistant protection, while SMS OTP — though better than no 2FA — is vulnerable to SIM swapping, SS7 interception, and real-time phishing proxies, making it unsuitable for high-value accounts.",
